  "description": "A parametric TV UNIT on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nTHE SCREEN IS SIZED FROM ITS DIAGONAL, the way screens are actually sold. A 16:9 panel is 0.87 × its diagonal wide and 0.49 tall, so one parameter gives the right rectangle and the published viewing distance (1.6 × the diagonal) is a figure someone can lay a sofa against. The screen is a separate piece at its own height, so a wall-mounted panel and the console below it are one object.\n\nTHE BAYS DIVIDE THE WIDTH, in the same bounded loop the chest of drawers uses for its fronts. One to six, and a 1.6 m console at three bays gives fronts of 533 mm without anyone doing the arithmetic.\n\nSHARES ITS CARCASS AND BASE with the nightstand and the chest — legs, plinth or wall-hung, written once for all three.",
